  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1952\n£10.00\n\nLow stock, 4 remaining\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1952 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O. Volume LIV January to December 1952.\n\nPublished 1953 - Slatter & Rose Oxford. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' 1951 -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed on December 31st, 1952 -p.12\n\nRecords of the First Battalion -p.14\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary 1952 -p.17\n\nFirst Battalion Letter -p.35\n\nSummary of First Battalion Sports Records -p.41\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters -p.43\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.44\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion -p.48\n\nFourth Battalion Letter -p.51\n\nRegimental Dinner 1952 -p.54\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner -p.55\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon -p.56\n\nOld Comrades Association -p.58\n\nHart's Army List, 1874-p.60\n\nSir Charles Rowan -p.62\n\nCentenary of the Wreck of the 'Birkenhead' -p.67\n\nKorean Interval -p.71\n\nDeir Mar Antonius -p.77\n\nFour Days in Sinai -p.85\n\n'Free Lance' -p.93\n\nObituary -p.98\n\nThe Regimental History Committee -p.102\n\nHistory of the 43rd Light Infantry 1867-1892 -p.104\n\nHistory of the 52nd Light Infantry 1859-1892 -p.162\n\nIndex -p.197\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre XI\n£4.99 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre IX\n£5.00 Add to cart\nRemembered: The Men on the War Memorials of Witney, Crawley and Hailey. Volume 2: 1939-1945.\n£9.99 Add to cart\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
